# Force the depth-first dependency collector.
#
# Workaround for a thread-safety bug in org.openntf.maven:p2-layout-resolver:1.9.0 (the p2 layout
# extension configured in uimaj-parent-internal). Its P2RepositoryLayout caches artifact metadata in
# plain java.util.HashMap fields; getPom() calls computeIfAbsent() on one of them with a mapping
# function that does substantial recursive work. That is safe only while descriptors are resolved
# sequentially.
#
# maven-resolver changed its default collector between Maven 3 and 4:
#   Maven 3.9.x / resolver 1.9.x -> DEFAULT_COLLECTOR_IMPL = "df" (depth-first, sequential)
#   Maven 4.0.x / resolver 2.0.x -> DEFAULT_COLLECTOR_IMPL = "bf" (breadth-first, parallel)
#
# Under "bf" several pool threads enter that computeIfAbsent concurrently and the build dies with a
# ConcurrentModificationException from HashMap, reported as an unresolvable plugin (the failing
# coordinate varies from run to run). Selecting "df" restores the Maven 3 behaviour and the build
# succeeds with the unmodified extension.
#
# Remove this once p2-layout-resolver makes those caches thread-safe; 1.9.0 is currently the newest
# published version. The cost of keeping it is losing the parallel collector's speed-up.
-Daether.dependencyCollector.impl=df
